   "evidence": "Distance.lean:86-111 provides `toIsometryEquiv_symm`, `toIsometryEquiv_refl` and `toIsometryEquiv_trans` for the coercion from `RiemannianIsometry` to `M \u2243\u1d62 N`. Smooth.lean adds the coercion's inverse `toRiemannianIsometry` but has no simp lemma for its composite with that coercion.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Riemannian/Isometry/Smooth.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem IsometryEquiv.toIsometryEquiv_toRiemannianIsometry (f : M \u2243\u1d62 N) : ((f.toRiemannianIsometry I J : RiemannianIsometry I J M N) : M \u2243\u1d62 N) = f := IsometryEquiv.ext fun _ \u21a6 (rfl)`. Optionally also add `@[simp] RiemannianIsometry.toRiemannianIsometry_toIsometryEquiv (\u03a6) : (\u03a6 : M \u2243\u1d62 N).toRiemannianIsometry I J = \u03a6`.",
   "issue": "`IsometryEquiv.toRiemannianIsometry` only has the function-level lemma `coe_toRiemannianIsometry`. Nothing simplifies the coercion back to an isometry equivalence, `((f.toRiemannianIsometry I J : RiemannianIsometry I J M N) : M \u2243\u1d62 N)`, to `f`. Because `isometryEquivEquiv_apply` rewrites `isometryEquivEquiv I J (f.toRiemannianIsometry I J)` into exactly this coercion, simp gets stuck there instead of closing the goal.",
   "line": 333
  }
